<div class="hero-section py-5 service-page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row align-items-center min-vh-50">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-8 text-start">
        <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-3" data-page-h1>
          From property address to offer price in minutes
        </h1>
        <p class="mb-0 hero-lead" style="max-width: 36rem">
          Feed it a property address. Get ARV, multiple exit strategies, a recommended offer price, and a plain English explanation, the way a senior acquisitions manager would explain it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="inner-sections">

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="problem">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row g-4 align-items-start">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-7">
          <h2 class="heading-border heading-center heading-left mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">The problem</h2>
          <p class="large-para mb-3">
            Real estate wholesalers and investors live and die by deal volume. The more properties they can analyze, the more deals they find. But accurate underwriting takes time, and experienced teams can spend significant time per property just to answer one question: is this worth making an offer on?
          </p>
          <p class="large-para mb-3">
            That means analysis capacity becomes the constraint, not deal flow. The bottleneck isn&rsquo;t finding properties. It&rsquo;s the analysis. Pulling the right comparable sales, calculating ARV correctly, running the numbers for multiple exit strategies, and deciding on an offer price, all of it requires experience, judgment, and time that most investors don&rsquo;t have enough of.
          </p>
          <p class="large-para mb-0">
            Junior analysts get the comps wrong. Spreadsheets don&rsquo;t explain their reasoning. And when a motivated seller is on the phone right now, there&rsquo;s no time to go run numbers in a separate tool before responding.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-5">
          <%= render "home/case_studies/at_a_glance",
            industry: "Real estate investing",
            client: "Confidential",
            country: "United Arab Emirates",
            what_we_built: "AI deal analyzer: ARV, exit strategies, offer price, and plain-English explanation",
            integrations: "ATTOM Data API, county assessor APIs",
            stack: "FastAPI (Python), Claude, Next.js, deterministic Python financial logic" %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey flow-lines-section"  id="what-we-built">
  <%= render "shared/flow_lines_background", tone: "gradient" %>
    <div class="container flow-lines-content">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block flow-lines-heading">What we built<span class="flow-lines-underline-ref" aria-hidden="true"></span></h2>
        <p class="large-para mb-3">
          An AI deal analyzer that takes a property address and structured data as input and outputs a complete investment analysis, ARV calculation with comp justification, four exit strategy projections, recommended offer price, profit potential, risk level, and a plain English explanation written the way an experienced acquisitions manager would explain it to a client.
        </p>
        <p class="large-para mb-0">
          Not a calculator. Not a spreadsheet. An analyst that works fast and never gets tired.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">How it works</h2>
        <ul class="service-page-list mb-4">
          <li><strong>Step 1 — Property data ingestion:</strong> The investor provides the property address and basic condition notes. The system pulls public records, tax history, and comparable sales data automatically via ATTOM Data API.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 2 — ARV with justified comp selection:</strong> Comparable sales are selected using appraiser-style criteria (radius, size, beds/baths, recency, condition adjustments), with narrative explaining which comps were included or excluded.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 3 — Four exit strategies:</strong> Wholesale (MAO), fix and flip, subject-to, and seller finance projections run side by side with profit, ROI, and risk flags against investor thresholds.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 4 — Plain English recommendation:</strong> The system recommends the strongest exit strategy, flags risk level, and outputs a natural language summary an acquisitions manager would give on a call.</li>
          <li><strong>Deterministic math layer:</strong> Python calculates every number using fixed, auditable formulas; Claude receives pre-calculated numbers and generates explanation only — offer prices cannot be hallucinated.</li>
          <li><strong>Comp scoring:</strong> Weighted filtering (distance, recency, size similarity, condition) before comps reach the AI narrative layer.</li>
          <li><strong>Investor configuration:</strong> Per-user thresholds (minimum flip margin, wholesale fee, cash-on-cash return) calibrate recommendations to each investor&rsquo;s strategy.</li>
          <li><strong>Stack:</strong> FastAPI backend, Claude reasoning layer, Next.js dashboard, structured JSON + PDF export, ATTOM and county assessor data sources.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="large-para mb-0">
          Explainability is a trust layer: every output shows comps selected, formula applied, assumptions used, and confidence level; investors can override inputs and rerun instantly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey track-lines-section"  id="results">
  <%= render "shared/track_lines_background", tone: "gradient" %>
    <div class="container track-lines-content">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto track-lines-grid">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">Results</h2>
        <ul class="service-page-list mb-0">
          <li>Deal analysis time reduced from lengthy manual work to a fast, repeatable workflow</li>
          <li>Investors analyze more deals per week without adding headcount</li>
          <li>Junior team members produce senior quality underwriting output from day one</li>
          <li>Fewer deals lost to slow response, investors give sellers an answer while still on the phone</li>
          <li>Offer accuracy improved, fewer overbids on marginal deals, fewer good deals passed on due to under analysis</li>
          <li>Acquisitions managers focus on negotiation and relationships instead of running spreadsheets</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%= render "home/case_studies/gallery", slug: "ai-deal-analyzer" %>
  <%= render "home/case_studies/client_quote", slug: "ai-deal-analyzer" %>
  <%= render "home/case_studies/cta", blurb: "We&rsquo;ll design a governed pipeline with deterministic math, explainable AI, and investor specific controls from day one." %>

  <section class="py-4 bg-white">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <%= link_to "Operations-heavy software →", industry_professional_services_path, class: "service-card-link ajax" %>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>